From: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: netns: use explicit initial namespace inode

The initial network namespace has a fixed inode number.  Calling
ns_common_init(&init_net) makes the generic helper expand a comparison of
&init_net with itself, which GCC 14 diagnoses as -Wtautological-compare under
-Werror.  Use the explicit-inum helper, matching the comment at the call site.

Signed-off-by: codeandsolder <codeandsolder@gmail.com>
---
--- a/net/core/net_namespace.c
+++ b/net/core/net_namespace.c
@@ -1282,7 +1282,7 @@ static int __init net_ns_init(void)
 	 * has a static inode number.
 	 */
 	preinit_net(&init_net, &init_user_ns);
-	if (ns_common_init(&init_net))
+	if (ns_common_init_inum(&init_net, NET_NS_INIT_INO))
 		panic("Could not preinitialize the initial network namespace");
 
 	down_write(&pernet_ops_rwsem);
